    :markdown
      _Loco_**Motion** recommends **Rails fixtures** for test data: named
      rows loaded in bulk and rolled back after every example, so the
      database work a spec needs is done once instead of every time.

.prose
  :markdown
    # Test Fixtures

    Every test needs records to act on, and how you make them decides how
    fast the suite runs once the schema grows. This guide covers why we use
    the fixtures built into Rails, how to set them up with RSpec, how to
    write them, the habits that keep a large fixture set healthy, and how to
    move an existing suite off factories one piece at a time.

